BT 1 0 0 1 0 56.8 Tm /F1 9.2 Tf 13.2 TL (A text reading such as "01530" preserves leading zeroes and needs d characters plus a terminating null byte.) Tj T* (Conversion with strtoul takes O\(d\) time for d digits; comparison of two strings is O\(d\) in the worst case. An integer) Tj T* (reading occupies a fixed-size object and arithmetic/comparison are O\(1\). Text uses O\(d\) space per reading; a 16-bit) Tj T* (integer uses a fixed 2-byte object on the target system. Text is useful for preserving the original display format, but it) Tj T* (must be validated and converted before arithmetic.) Tj T* ET
